sorted´Returns a new sorted list containing all the elements of the supplied iterable sequence. An error may occur if any pair of elements x, y may not be compared using x < y. The elements are sorted into ascending order, unless the reverse argument is True, in which case the order is descending.
 Sorting is stable: elements that compare equal retain their original relative order.

```
sorted([3, 5, 4]) == [3, 4, 5]
sorted([3, 5, 4], reverse = True) == [5, 4, 3]
sorted(["two", "three", "four"], key = len) == ["two", "four", "three"]  # sort by length

```*¸
