configuration_field¥[`.bzl` only] References a late-bound default value for an attribute of type [label](../toplevel/attr.html#label). A value is 'late-bound' if it requires the configuration to be built before determining the value. Any attribute using this as a value must [be private](https://bazel.build/extending/rules#private-attributes).

Example usage:

Defining a rule attribute:

```
'_foo': attr.label(default=configuration_field(fragment='java', name='toolchain'))
```

Accessing in rule implementation:

```
  def _rule_impl(ctx):
    foo_info = ctx.attr._foo
    ...
```*Ä
