`exec_group`€Label‡[`.bzl` only] Converts a label string into a `Label` object, in the context of the package where the calling `.bzl` source file lives. If the given value is already a `Label`, it is returned unchanged.

For macros, a related function, `native.package_relative_label()`, converts the input into a `Label` in the context of the package currently being constructed. Use that function to mimic the string-to-label conversion that is automatically done by label-valued rule attributes.*Ï
