`string`óctx.expand_make_variablesì**Deprecated.** Use [ctx.var](../builtins/ctx.html#var) to access the variables instead.

Returns a string after expanding all references to "Make variables". The variables must have the following format: `$(VAR_NAME)`. Also, `$$VAR_NAME` expands to `$VAR_NAME`. Examples:

```
ctx.expand_make_variables("cmd", "$(MY_VAR)", {"MY_VAR": "Hi"})  # == "Hi"
ctx.expand_make_variables("cmd", "$$PWD", {})  # == "$PWD"

```

Additional variables may come from other places, such as configurations. Note that this function is experimental.Ç<ctx>.expand_make_variables*√
