`int`ëstring.format¸Perform string interpolation. Format strings contain replacement fields surrounded by curly braces `{}`. Anything that is not contained in braces is considered literal text, which is copied unchanged to the output.If you need to include a brace character in the literal text, it can be escaped by doubling: `{{` and `}}` A replacement field can be either a name, a number, or empty. Values are converted to strings using the [str](../globals/all.html#str) function.

```
# Access in order:
"{} < {}".format(4, 5) == "4 < 5"
# Access by position:
"{1}, {0}".format(2, 1) == "1, 2"
# Access by name:
"x{key}x".format(key = 2) == "x2x"
```Ç<string>.format*Ï
